The copy constructor already does the minimum work: it copies the base class and four small members. The real cost is in `FieldBase`'s copy, which this function cannot change.

This version keeps the same behavior and member initialization order. The only change is in the body. That empty-body edit is cosmetic and should not measurably change decode time.

```cpp
Field::Field(const Field &field)
    : FieldBase(field),
      profile(field.profile),
      profileIndex(field.profileIndex),
      type(field.type),
      isFieldExpanded(field.isFieldExpanded)
{
    // Trivially copied members; all work done in the initializer list.
}
```